# Agent Context — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

This file is the entry point for any AI agent working in this repo. `CLAUDE.md` is just
`@AGENTS.md`, so everything an agent needs to know starts here.

## Always

- Read this file first. Match your task against the **Task Router** below and load the listed
  context before writing any code.
- Use the canonical helpers and components the project already provides; reuse before you build.
- Run the project's verification gate — every command in `framework.config.json` → `validation` —
  before declaring work done. Treat any non-zero exit as a failure to fix.
- After a correction, record a durable rule in `.ai/lessons.md` so the same mistake doesn't recur.

## Ask first

- Applying database migrations or any destructive/irreversible operation.
- Adding a new dependency, service, or external integration.
- Anything outward-facing (opening PRs, posting comments, sending data off the machine).

## Never

- Edit generated output or `node_modules` directly.
- Hard-code colors, sizes, secrets, or environment-specific paths.
- Commit directly to `git.defaultBranch` — branch first.
- Roll your own substitute for a concern the project already has a canonical mechanism for.

## Validation

The verification gate is defined in `framework.config.json` → `validation`. Run it in full; it is
all-or-nothing. Paths (`modulesRoot`, `specsRoot`, `testsRoot`) come from the same config.

## Task Router

Match your task, then **stop and read the listed file(s)** before writing code. A task may match
multiple rows — load all of them.

