> Adapter packs (e.g. `open-mercato`) inject additional rows into the `TASK_ROUTER` region above
> at render time. Keep the markers intact.

## Core principles

- Concise context is a public good — load only what the task needs.
- Prefer the smallest change that satisfies the spec; don't refactor unrelated code.
- Validate all inputs; keep types explicit at boundaries.
- Make behaviour observable and testable.

## Stack

Resolve specifics from `framework.config.json` (`stack`, `orm`, `ui`, `harnesses`). This skeleton
is stack-agnostic; the installed adapter pack fills in the project's concrete conventions.
